\title{Beyond Nova: HyperNova, ProtoStar, ProtoGalaxy}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The folding design space after Nova: which constraint systems can be folded, how many instances
    at once, and what the recursive circuit costs.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{HyperNova: folding [CCS](dhsorens-002V), with per-step cost dominated by one MSM.}
        \li{ProtoStar: folding arbitrary low-degree polynomial maps, and what that generality buys.}
        \li{ProtoGalaxy and multi-instance folding; KiloNova and non-uniform PCD.}
        \li{The axes to compare on: constraint system, instances per fold, recursive circuit size,
        assumptions.}
        \li{Which of these is the right target for a formalisation, given that the definitions are
        still moving.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: [HyperNova](https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/573), [multi-instance folding
    techniques](https://hackmd.io/@fluentlabs/multi-instance-folding-techniques),
    [awesome-folding](https://github.com/lurk-lab/awesome-folding).
}
